  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_001, RNA-only/PCA/single-profile) yielded a low accuracy of ~48.5%, leaving major uncertainty about whether the image modality provides complementary or superior signal. Testing image_only with a standard pretrained ResNet50 (config_010) isolates the image modality's contribution without confounding from multiprofile, aggregation, or fusion. If image alone achieves comparable or better accuracy, it validates investing remaining budget in multimodal fusion; if it is also poor, it suggests the bottleneck lies in representation quality (motivating scGPT/scVI tests) rather than modality choice. This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves a binary question—does image carry useful signal?—that fundamentally reshapes the search strategy for the remaining 8 experiments."
}

